From 6cafb7a386d3a17cb6be1b2fda89c4bf2f9c6419 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:00:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(chunks): recover unacknowledged join radius requests

Protocol 2193 captures from the macOS CubeCraft regression show a join
remaining before spawn with no radius acknowledgment or level chunks at
radius four. Repeating four did not start delivery; requesting eight on
the same connection immediately yielded the acknowledgment, chunks,
spawn, initialization, and sustained input frames.

Preserve the Java distance for the initial request. Retry once after five
seconds, then use radius eight only for an unacknowledged smaller radius.
Bound the negotiation to thirty seconds, cancel on acknowledgment or
spawn, and replace pending retries when settings change. Keep this in
core for direct and ViaProxy routes. This is server interoperability
recovery, not a claim that native Bedrock always requires radius eight.
